<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kansas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kansas is a state of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, lying on the Great Plains between Missouri and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a>. Its grasslands were hunting grounds of the Kansa, Osage, Pawnee, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a> and others. Opened to settlement in 1854, it became the scene of violent clashes between pro- and anti-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> settlers known as Bleeding Kansas, before joining the Union as a free state in 1861.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kansas.jpg" alt="Kansas" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Xrmap · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kansas.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
